Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Azimuth Flutter Across the Nave
- Story & Context: During a frozen January vigil at Saint-Lazare, Brother Cyprian spilled scalding beeswax directly into the tape transport of an open Studer reel machine while transcribing an elder monk’s sleep-state telemetry. The hardened wax dragged the capstan into an irregular, fluttering limp, turning what was meant to be a straightforward hymn into an obsessive, stumbling cycle of choked cowbells and brittle nylon strings. When the Abbot threatened to smash the synthesizer racks for profaning the chapel, Cyprian leaned into the whirring tape motor and whispered into the cold air, "The ribbon holds what our knees forgot." The surviving tape survived as the bootleg foundation of the entire Pyrenean circuit.
