Track 2: Did You Burn the Reel-to-Reel, Anselm?
- Story & Context: Anselm fled the cloister at midnight carrying two stolen sleep-voltage patch maps and an unlacquered copper cowbell in a flour sack, finding refuge in the cellar of an abandoned cheese dairy near Les Baronnies. Sister Odile tracked him through the snow, carrying a dead magnesium flashlamp and demanding the return of the order's dream journals before the parish council noticed the theft. In the pitch darkness, Anselm struck the bell with an iron hinge and murmured his confession across the damp stone floor: "You cannot pray away the current under my tongue." Rather than dragging him back to the chapel, Odile sat on an overturned salt tub and joined his trance, harmonizing through her chapped lips until sunrise.
